    "narrative": "The primary engine for LawDog\u2019s production today is **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who commands the highest score (76.64) due to an elite combination of a high-ceiling park factor (+14%) and a favorable matchup against Gordon. His ability to capitalize on the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery makes him our premier SB threat. **Dylan Beavers** (69.52) and **Lawrence Butler** (69.21) also project as foundational pieces; both benefit from significant platoon advantages and opportunistic pairings with Wesneski and Peralta, respectively. **Bryce Harper** (68.61) rounds out the high-leverage tier, maintaining an impressive .391 xwOBA that signals sustained production against Dobbins.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Justin Crawford** on the bench. Despite his sprint speed and a respectable 55.60 score, **Justin Crawford** was relegated to the bench because his projected #9 spot in the lineup severely throttles his run-scoring potential compared to the high-order density of **Gleyber Torres** (64.10) and **JJ Bleday** (68.50). While **Justin Crawford** offers a high floor for SB, the optimizer prioritized the volume and efficiency of the starting outfield. We are monitoring **Brendan Donovan** and **JJ Bleday** closely, as their scores are based on assumed batting orders; should either drop down the lineup, their efficiency scores will likely retract, though **JJ Bleday**\u2019s 14% platoon edge against Rodriguez provides a solid buffer. \n\nBeyond lineup volatility, owners should note that **Cal Raleigh** and **Brendan Donovan** face the veteran arm of Boyd. While the platoon dynamics are favorable, Boyd remains a pitcher capable of suppressing power. Elsewhere, **Yainer Diaz** and **Zack Gelof** are functioning as marginal starts; their scores remain in the mid-50s, highlighting the need for them to capitalize on immediate plate appearance efficiency to avoid wasting valuable roster spots. With **Tyler Freeman**, **Will Smith**, and **Matt Chapman** confirmed on the IL, we have zero margin for error regarding game caps today.",
